A PGP signature is not a .sig file and has never been a part of the
4-line etiquette limit.  It is specific to the particular message it
signs and is a functional unit; a good newsreader won't display it
(it'll display the signed message and either a note that it's been
verified, rejected, or uses an unknown key).

The sig-dashes are broken as you indicate (the protocol is a single
line consisting of two dashes and a space: "-- ").



